From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pessi-v <pessimo@posteo.net>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:54:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] (hybris) vold: do not start

Sailfish OS mounts storage itself (udisks2 for removable media), and
nothing on this adaptation uses Android's volume manager. vold only
unmounts what it finds under /mnt at start and fails; on some builds its
service carries reboot_on_failure.
---
 vold.rc |    1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/vold.rc b/vold.rc
index 93d878663bdd6cd51cbd951e9a54cac3c75f8e72..9a04576a122c01b1d60c517a49f5bd0eb217c43b 100644
--- a/vold.rc
+++ b/vold.rc
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@ service vold /system/bin/vold \
         --blkid_context=u:r:blkid:s0 --blkid_untrusted_context=u:r:blkid_untrusted:s0 \
         --fsck_context=u:r:fsck:s0 --fsck_untrusted_context=u:r:fsck_untrusted:s0
     class core
+    disabled
     ioprio be 2
     writepid /dev/cpuset/foreground/tasks
     shutdown critical
